    {
      "id": "p0114-b005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Unfortunately, the Papyrus font doesn't support Japanese characters, nor does the Japanese language have capital letters. So, to ensure that Papyrus' text remained visually weird, funny, and memorable in Japanese, 8-4's technical team redesigned Papyrus' dialogue boxes to display text in Japanese tate style (vertically from top to bottom, moving right to left) instead of horizontally. The result is immediately striking and reinforces the idea that Papyrus is a happy go-lucky oddball who's oblivious to the world around him.",
        "raw": "Unfortunately, the Papyrus font doesn't support Japanese characters, nor does\nthe Japanese language have capital letters. So, to ensure that Papyrus' text\nremained visually weird, funny, and memorable in Japanese, 8-4's technical\nteam redesigned Papyrus' dialogue boxes to display text in Japanese tate style\n(vertically from top to bottom, moving right to left) instead of horizontally. The\nresult is immediately striking and reinforces the idea that Papyrus is a happy\ngo-lucky oddball who's oblivious to the world around him.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29388326,
          0.36853571,
          0.90357377,
          0.49073571
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.2871837,
          0.36782143,
          0.90713259,
          0.49180714
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          20,
          22,
          24,
          26,
          28,
          29,
          30
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "可惜 Papyrus 字体不支持日文，日语也没有大写字母。因此，为了让 Papyrus 的台词在日语中依然显得古怪、有趣、令人难忘，8-4 技术团队重新设计了他的对话框，采用日语 tate（竖排）形式：字由上往下，列由右往左，不再横排。效果立刻就很醒目，也进一步突出了 Papyrus 乐天、古怪、对周围世界浑然不觉的性格。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
          {
            "start": 90,
            "end": 94,
            "italic": true,
            "lang": "en"
          }
        ]
      },
